Unique Numbers 10

Given two integers L and R, print all numbers between L and R (inclusive) which contain all unique digits. A number is called unique if no digit repeats within the number.

Input Format

• Two space-separated integers: L and R

Constraints

• 1 ≤ L ≤ R ≤ 10⁴

Output Format

• Print all unique numbers between L and R, separated by a space, in a single line.

Sample Input 0

98 102
Sample Output 0

98 102
Explanation 0

Explanation: 99, 100, 101 all have repeated digits.

Sample Input 1

120 130
Sample Output 1

120 123 124 125 126 127 128 129 130
Explanation 1

Explanation: 121 and 122 have repeated digits.
